+## Run with Docker
+
+If you don't have Node.js installed or you have heightened security requirements, you can run Doc Detective in a Docker container instead of installing it with npm. The Docker image is in alpha and isn't ready for production use.
+
+1. Install prerequisites:
+
+    - [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/)
+
+2. In a terminal, pull the Doc Detective Docker image:
+
+    ```bash
+    docker pull docdetective/doc-detective
+    ```
+
+3. Save the same _sample.spec.json_ file from the previous section to your current directory.
+
+4. Run a test, mounting your current directory into the container so Doc Detective can read your test file and write results back to your machine:
+
+    ```bash
+    docker run --rm -v "$(pwd)":/app docdetective/doc-detective --input sample.spec.json
+    ```
+
+    On Windows, replace `$(pwd)` with `%cd%`.
+
+Congratulations! You've run your first test with Doc Detective in Docker. :tada:
+
+Results are saved in a `testResults-<timestamp>.json` file in your current directory (configurable with the `--output` option), and this test saves a screenshot to example.png.
+
+:::note
+
+The Docker image is in alpha. For more information, see the [`docker-image` repository](https://github.com/doc-detective/docker-image).
+
+:::
+
